 woman"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மான்பிணை","parts":[{"text":"மான்","lemma":"மான்","gloss":"deer"},{"text":"பிணை","lemma":"பிணை","gloss":"female"}],"gloss":"female deer"},{"surface":"யன்ன","parts":[{"text":"யன்ன","lemma":"யன்ன","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மகிழ்மட","parts":[{"text":"மகிழ்மட","lemma":"மகிழ்மட","gloss":"joyful and innocent"}],"gloss":"joyful and innocent","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நோக்கே","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கு","lemma":"நோக்கு","gloss":"gaze"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"gaze"}]}],"literal":"Even if kings and leaders come, they will not cease to resist / So that the spears with rows of strong shafts plunge like water / Because noble warriors have joined, the father also will turn them back / At the pond near the gate of the fertile paddy fields / Where the stork, eating kayal fish, startles the vaalai fish / Which the water-playing women carry to their prosperous homes / Will this town lose its beauty? / The young woman with young breasts adorned with beauty spots, rising and prominent / With full wrists and bamboo-like shoulders / And a joyful, innocent gaze like that of a female deer.","translation":"Even if great kings march against him, he will never yield. The father will turn them back, aided by noble warriors, making their spears with strong shafts plunge into the enemy like water. In this town, at the pond near the gates of fertile fields, storks feeding on kayal fish startle the vaalai fish, which women playing in the water carry back to their prosperous homes. Will this beautiful town be ruined and lose its splendor for the sake of this young woman, whose rising, prominent breasts are adorned with beauty spots, who has full wrists, bamboo-like shoulders, and a joyful, innocent gaze like that of a gentle doe?","modern":"அரசர்களே திரண்டு வந்தாலும் பணிய மாட்டார். சிறந்த வீரர்கள் வந்து சேர்ந்ததால், பெண்ணின் தந்தையும் பகைவரைத் திருப்பி அனுப்புவார்; வரிசையான வலிமையான காம்புகளைக் கொண்ட வேல்கள் தண்ணீரில் மூழ்குவது போலப் பகைவர் உடலில் மூழ்கும். வயல்களின் வாயிலில் உள்ள பொய்கையில், கயல் மீன்களை உண்ணும் நாரை விரட்டிய வாளை மீனை, நீராடும் மகளிர் பிடித்துத் தங்கள் வளமான வீடுகளுக்குக் கொண்டு செல்வர். இத்தகைய அழகிய ஊர் தன் பொலிவை இழக்கப் போகிறதோ? தேமல் அணிந்த, நிமிர்ந்து ஏந்திய இளமுலைகளையும், பருத்த மணிக்கட்டுகளையும், மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களையும் கொண்ட இப்பெண்ணின், பெண் மான் போன்ற மகிழ்ச்சியான மடப்பம் நிறைந்த பார்வைக்காக!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the kāñci tiṇai and specifically the makaṭpāṟ kāñci tuṟai, which depicts the tragic situation where a king demands a beautiful girl in marriage, but her proud father and kinsmen refuse, leading to a devastating war that threatens to destroy the entire town. The poet Paranar vividly contrasts the peaceful, fertile landscape of the town with the impending violence of war. The imagery of the stork chasing the vāḷai fish, which is then easily caught by bathing women, symbolizes the abundance and vulnerability of the town. The father's fierce pride is highlighted by his readiness to fight off even great kings, ensuring that their spears plunge into the enemy like water. Ultimately, the poem laments how the innocent, deer-like gaze of a young woman can become the catalyst for the destruction of a beautiful and prosperous settlement.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.72],[1.72,2.01],[2.01,2.59],[2.59,3.1],[3.1,3.6],[3.6,4.1],[4.1,5.0],[5.0,5.4],[5.4,5.9],[5.9,6.1],[6.1,7.3],[7.3,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,8.5],[8.5,8.83],[8.83,9.0],[9.11,9.56],[9.56,9.78],[10.0,11.0],[11.0,11.5],[11.5,11.9],[11.9,12.52],[12.52,13.3],[13.3,13.9],[13.9,14.3],[14.3,14.5],[14.7,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.1,16.6],[16.78,17.4],[17.6,17.8],[18.64,19.54],[19.54,19.94],[19.94,20.44],[20.44,20.89],[20.89,21.23],[21.23,21.8],[21.8,22.14]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.3],[1.3,1.82],[1.91,2.29],[2.29,3.04],[3.04,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.02],[4.02,4.77],[4.77,5.9],[5.9,6.5],[6.5,7.4],[7.4,8.3],[8.3,8.8],